+# Todo Due Dates and Overdue Filters Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Give todos optional API-managed due dates and matching overdue filters in the API and list page for ticket `adw/demo-todo#1`.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the shared, locked in-memory store as the source of truth. Use `DateOnly?` for dates, explicit PATCH field presence, and an injectable `TimeProvider` for current UTC-derived response snapshots. Blazor reads the store directly and applies the same filter through a checkbox.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, ASP.NET Core minimal APIs, interactive server Blazor, System.Text.Json, xUnit, WebApplicationFactory, Playwright MCP. No new NuGet packages.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-14-todo-due-date-design.md` (user approved and posted as Approved Spec on ticket 1).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- JSON uses `YYYY-MM-DD` or `null`; dates have no time component.
+- Today is the current UTC date. Only open todos with a date before today are overdue.
+- PATCH omission preserves the date; explicit `null` removes it.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos; absent or `false` returns all.
+- Exact UI copy: `nur überfällige` for the checkbox and `überfällig` for the marker.
+- Dates appear next to titles. No creation/edit forms, sorting, reminders, styling work, timers, or new push updates.
+- Keep `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`; add `todo-overdue-filter`, `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`.
+- Keep ValidationException-based store validation, JSON HTTP 400 errors, existing status codes, ID order, and singleton storage.
+- Run TDD under `tests/`; no new NuGet packages. Agent performs E2E with Playwright MCP; screenshots outside the repo; stop the started app.
+- Work on `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; base `main`. Open a draft PR via tea; do not merge, publish, or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Empty PATCH and independent title/done changes must preserve an existing date; reopening a past-due todo restores its overdue status (Tasks 1–2).
+2. A UTC midnight crossing, including a clock value with a nonzero offset, must refresh output and filtering without writes; one list uses one time reading (Task 1).
+3. Invalid or wrongly typed date JSON must not partially update a valid title or create a todo (Task 2).
+4. Titles containing HTML must remain escaped when dates and markers are added (Task 3).
+5. Keyboard/label activation of the checkbox must handle empty results and restore the full list when switched off (Task 3 E2E).
+
